  "body": "Using the DataTransfer API you can make data travel across security boundaries - web to local application. This can enable malicious payloads - for example malformed data intended to exploit bugs in data processing of local applications that are targets of Drag-and-drop or copy/paste operations.\n\nFor better or worse, we have to consider these issues. Implementations are already adding security precautions that are not covered by the current spec, such as \n- Allowing only a limited number of white-listed types to map to their \"native type\" on the os clipboard. Other types are bundled up inside a browser-specific \"our custom data\" field.\n- Transcoding image data to ensure what gets written to the clipboard is sane\n\nThe algorithms in the spec need to add such measures for security reasons.\n",
